Only machine-facing markers and command names (gentle-ai -> amauta) were
adapted; prose content is kept as upstream wrote it. The upstream license text
is reproduced below as required by that license.

The optional SDD module (assets/sdd/) comes from the v3.4.0 release of the same
project (skills, agents, commands and shared contracts, MIT). Differences: commands
are renamed /gentle-sdd-* -> /amauta-sdd-*, calls to the compiled `gentle-ai sdd-*`
commands point at amauta.sdd, and the native archive composer section is
replaced by a manual-composition note.

The optional design skill assets/skills/impeccable/ is vendored from impeccable, which is
distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text in
assets/skills/impeccable/LICENSE):

  Project:  pbakaus/impeccable
  URL:      https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable
  Tag:      skill-v3.9.1 (path .claude/skills/impeccable)
  Commit:   44c27a72af98394c32691ba79358811bff86bde6
  Engine:   impeccable@3.6.1 from npm (installed on demand with --with-impeccable, not vendored)

Changes made by amauta: the project-local skill paths in the markdown were replaced by
placeholders resolved at install time; the `pin`, `unpin` and `hooks` commands and their scripts
(pin.mjs, hook*.mjs, reference/hooks.md) were removed; the once-a-day update check in
scripts/context.mjs was disabled; the `allowed-tools` frontmatter was dropped. Everything else is
as upstream published it.

